      "body": "## What\n\n`_generate_request_id_base()` in `serving_base.py` returns `None` unconditionally, so the code below it could never run:\n\n```python\nreturn None\n\n# TODO(chang): the rid is used in io_strcut check and often violates ...\nif rid := getattr(request, \"rid\", None):\n    return rid\n\nreturn f\"{self._request_id_prefix()}{uuid.uuid4().hex}\"\n```\n\nThe `uuid` import exists only for that unreachable line. Anything added under the `return None` inherits the same problem, which is how this survived: the deferral note reads like an explanation of live code.\n\n## Change\n\n- Move the TODO up as a comment on `return None` so the deferral is still documented where the implementation will go.\n- Delete the unreachable tail and the now-unused `uuid` import.\n\nNo behaviour change: the method returned `None` before and returns `None` after. `_request_id_prefix` is left alone — it is called live by the OCR streaming path (`models/unlimited_ocr_v2_support/chat.py`) and several serving classes, and the removed line was not its only user.\n\n## Scope\n\nSingle file, +4/−8, no test. The earlier revision of this PR added an `ast` test asserting that no statement follows the unconditional return; it has been dropped. That guard is closer to a linter than a test — it pins one private method's name and shape for 55 lines — and the shape it protected is now simply gone.\n\n`black --check` and `ruff check --select F,E9` are clean on the file.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41826333793](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41826333793)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41826333704](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41826333704)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41826333612](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41826333612)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
